rds if word not in stop_words]\n    \n    return ' '.join(words)\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2025-05-02T09:15:28.371102Z","iopub.execute_input":"2025-05-02T09:15:28.371549Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-05-02T09:15:28.378885Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2025-05-02T09:15:28.371525Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-05-02T09:15:28.377830Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":37},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**4.3: Apply Cleaning to Entire Dataset**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Apply text cleaning to all documents\ncleaned_text_data = combined_text_data.apply(clean_text)\n\n# Preview first few cleaned samples\nprint(\"🧪 Sample Cleaned Texts:\")\nfor i in range(5):\n    print(f\"{i+1}. {cleaned_text_data[i][:150]}...\\n\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2025-05-02T09:15:28.379934Z","iopub.execute_input":"2025-05-02T09:15:28.380193Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-05-02T09:15:33.858351Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2025-05-02T09:15:28.380172Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-05-02T09:15:33.857304Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"🧪 Sample Cleaned Texts:\n1. third volume handbook covers whole field soil mechanics discussing deterministic stochastic theories methods showing used conjunction one another firs...\n\n2. residual soils found many parts world like soils used extensively construction built upon used construction materials residual soils formed processes ...\n\n3. volume brings together papers geotechnical civil engineers biologists ecologists foresters discuss current problems slope stability research address u...\n\n4. recent years international society soil mechanics geotechnical engineering issmge international association engineering geology environment iaeg inter...\n\n5. textbook provides overview transport fate processes environmental contamination way reader understand predict contaminant patterns soil groundwater su...\n\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":38},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**4.4: Summary of Cleaning Operations**\n\n| Step               | Purpose                                       |\n| ------------------ | --------------------------------------------- |\n| Remove Punctuation | Reduces noise for vector models               |\n| Lowercase          | Improves semantic consistency                 |\n| Remove Stopwords   | Focuses on meaningful words for search        |\n| Concatenation      | Merges multiple sources for diverse knowledge |\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Part 5: Embedding + FAISS Vector Indexing\n\nGoal: Convert cleaned text into semantic embeddings and index them using FAISS for fast vector similarity search.\nThis enables powerful RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) with Gemini.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**5.1: Load Sentence Embedding Model**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"from sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer\n\n# Load the model (switch to device='cuda' if running on GPU)\nembed_model = SentenceTransformer('all-MiniLM-L6-v2', device='cpu')\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2025-05-02T09:15:33.859367Z","iopub.execute_input":"2025-05-02T09:15:33.859647Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-05-02T09:15:35.322725Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2025-05-02T09:15:33.859628Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-05-02T09:15:35.321836Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":39},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**5.2: Generate Embeddings**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Encode all text entries into vector representations\nprint(\"⚙️ Generating sentence embeddings...\")\n\ntext_embeddings = embed_model.encode(\n    cleaned_text_data.tolist(),\n    show_progress_bar=True,\n    convert_to_numpy=True\n)\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2025-05-02T09:15:35.323784Z","iopub.execute_input":"2025-05-02T09:15:35.324118Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"⚙️ Generating sentence embeddings...\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"Batches:   0%|          | 0/885 [00:00<?, ?it/s]","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id":"123f150c38cb4faf97e66fec1440029f"}},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**5.3: Normalize and Build FAISS Index**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"import faiss\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Normalize vectors to unit length (improves search)\nfaiss.normalize_L2(text_embeddings)\n\n# Create FAISS index with L2 distance\ndimension = text_embeddings.shape[1]\nindex = faiss.IndexFlatL2(dimension)\n\n# Add vectors to index\nindex.add(text_embeddings)\n\n# Save index to disk (optional)\nfaiss.write_index(index, \"book_index.faiss\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**5.4: Define a Basic Search Function**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def semantic_search(query: str, k: int = 5):\n    \"\"\"Search FAISS index and return top k most relevant texts.\"\"\"\n    query_vector = embed_model.encode([clean_text(query)]).astype(\"float32\")\n    faiss.normalize_L2(query_vector)\n    distances, indices = index.search(query_vector, k)\n\n    return [cleaned_text_data[i] for i in indices[0]]\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**5.5: Test the Search**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"results = semantic_search(\"deep learning in computer vision\")\n\nprint(\"🔎 Search Results:\")\nfor i, result in enumerate(results, 1):\n    print(f\"\\nResult {i}:\\n{result[:300]}{'...' if len(result) > 300 else ''}\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"| Component        | Value                    |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------ |\n| Model Used       | `all-MiniLM-L6-v2`       |\n| Total Vectors    | `{len(text_embeddings)}` |\n| Vector Dimension | `{dimension}`            |\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Part 6: Semantic Search (Verbose + RAG Support)\n\nGoal: Build an advanced RAG-compatible search tool that:\n\nNormalizes distance scores into similarity percentages\n\nProvides top-k relevant snippets\n\nPrepares output for Gemini grounding","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**6.1: Verbose RAG Search Function**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def rag_search_verbose(query: str, k: int = 5) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Perform semantic search and return verbose, readable output.\n    \n    Args:\n        query: User's natural language question\n        k: Number of top results to return\n    \n    Returns:\n        A formatted string with similarity scores and matched texts\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        # Step 1: Clean and embed the query\n        cleaned_query = clean_text(query)\n        query_embedding = embed_model.encode([cleaned_query]).astype(\"float32\")\n        faiss.normalize_L2(query_embedding)\n\n        # Step 2: Search FAISS index\n        distances, indices = index.search(query_embedding, k)\n        \n        # Normalize distances to similarity (0=most similar)\n        max_dist = max(distances[0].max(), 1e-6)  # avoid divide by 0\n        similarity_scores = 1 - (distances[0] / (max_dist + 1e-6))\n\n        # Step 3: Format results\n        results = []\n        for i, (idx, score) in enumerate(zip(indices[0], similarity_scores), 1):\n            text = cleaned_text_data.iloc[idx]\n            snippet = text[:300].strip() + (\"...\" if len(text) > 300 else \"\")\n            results.append(f\"Result {i} [Similarity: {score:.1%}]\\n{snippet}\")\n\n        return \"\\n\\n\" + \"─\" * 50 + \"\\n\\n\".join(results) + \"\\n\" + \"─\" * 50\n\n    except Exception as e:\n        return f\"❌ Search failed: {str(e)}\"\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**6.2: Example Usage**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Try a RAG-style verbose search\nquery = \"neural networks in computer vision\"\nprint(rag_search_verbose(query, k=3))\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"| Feature           | Value                                     |\n| ----------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| Preprocessing     | `clean_text()` on query                   |\n| Embedding         | `SentenceTransformer` vector              |\n| Similarity metric | FAISS L2 → normalized to 0–100% match     |\n| Output            | Top-k matches with similarity scores      |\n| Output formatting | Text preview + ellipsis + separation bars |\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Part 7: Document Extraction (PDF, Excel, YouTube)\n\nGoal: Extract clean text from multiple file types to feed into GenAI summarization or semantic search pipelines.\nSupported formats:\n\nPDF files (scanned textbooks or notes)\n\nExcel files (structured tables, MCQs)\n\nYouTube videos (transcript-based)","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**7.1: Extract Text from PDF**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"import pdfplumber\nimport os\n\ndef extract_pdf_text(file_path: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extract text from a PDF file using pdfplumber.\n    \n    Args:\n        file_path: Full path to the PDF file\n    \n    Returns:\n        Extracted text as a string or error message\n    \"\"\"\n    if not os.path.exists(file_path):\n        return f\"❌ File not found: {file_path}\"\n\n    try:\n        with pdfplumber.open(file_path) as pdf:\n            pages = [page.extract_text() or \"\" for page in pdf.pages]\n        return \"\\n\".join(pages).strip()\n    except Exception as e:\n        return f\"❌ Error reading PDF: {str(e)}\"\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**7.2: Extract Text from Excel Files**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"import pandas as pd\n\ndef extract_excel_text(file) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extract and flatten text from all sheets of an Excel file.\n    \n    Args:\n        file: File-like object (e.g., upload or open() result)\n    \n    Returns:\n        Combined sheet content or error message\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        # Read all sheets into a dictionary\n        excel_data = pd.read_excel(file, sheet_name=None)\n        text_chunks = []\n\n        for sheet_name, df in excel_data.items():\n            sheet_text = \"\\n\".join(df.astype(str).fillna('').values.flatten().tolist())\n            if sheet_text.strip():\n                text_chunks.append(f\"--- Sheet: {sheet_name} ---\\n{sheet_text}\")\n        \n        final_text = \"\\n\\n\".join(text_chunks).strip()\n        return final_text if final_text else \"❌ No extractable text found in Excel file.\"\n    except Exception as e:\n        return f\"❌ Error reading Excel file: {str(e)}\"\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**7.3: Extract Transcript from YouTube Videos**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"from youtube_transcript_api import YouTubeTranscriptApi\n\ndef extract_text_from_youtube(url: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extract transcript from a YouTube video using the transcript API.\n    \n    Args:\n        url: Full YouTube video URL\n    \n    Returns:\n        Combined transcript or error message\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        match = re.search(r\"v=([A-Za-z0-9_-]{11})\", url)\n        if not match:\n            return \"❌ Could not extract video ID from URL.\"\n        \n        video_id = match.group(1)\n        transcript = YouTubeTranscriptApi.get_transcript(video_id, languages=['en'])\n\n        if not transcript:\n            return \"❌ No English transcript found.\"\n        \n        return \"\\n\".join([segment['text'] for segment in transcript])\n    except Exception as e:\n        return f\"❌ Error: {str(e)}\"\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Part 8: Summarization + Flashcard Generator (Structured Output)\n\nGoal: Use Gemini to:\n\nGenerate a summary of input text\n\nGenerate revision flashcards in structured Q&A format\n\nParse results into clean Python objects","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**8.1: Function to Summarize and Generate Flashcards**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def summarize_and_flashcards(text: str, max_flashcards: int = 30) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generate a summary and flashcards from educational text using Gemini.\n    \n    Args:\n        text: Source content to summarize\n        max_flashcards: Number of flashcards to generate (default=30)\n    \n    Returns:\n        Dictionary with 'summary', 'flashcards', and 'error' keys\n    \"\"\"\n    result = {\"summary\": \"\", \"flashcards\": [], \"error\": None}\n\n    try:\n        prompt = f\"\"\"**StudyMate Task**\n\n=== SUMMARY ===\nCreate a concise 3-5 sentence summary of the content:\n\n{text[:3000]}\n\n=== FLASHCARDS ===\nGenerate {max_flashcards} flashcards in the format:\n\nQ: [Clear conceptual question]\nA: [Short answer under 20 words]\n\nRules:\n1. No markdown formatting\n2. Questions must be answerable using the input content\n\"\"\"\n\n        response = gemini_model.generate_content(prompt)\n\n        if not response.text:\n            raise ValueError(\"Empty response from Gemini.\")\n\n        # Split into sections\n        sections = response.text.split(\"=== FLASHCARDS ===\")\n        result[\"summary\"] = sections[0].strip() if len(sections) > 0 else \"\"\n        if len(sections) > 1:\n            result[\"flashcards\"] = extract_flashcards_from_text(sections[1])\n\n    except Exception as e:\n        result[\"error\"] = f\"Processing failed: {str(e)}\"\n\n    return result\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**8.2: Helper to Extract Flashcards from Gemini Output**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def extract_flashcards_from_text(text: str) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Parse flashcard-style Q&A pairs from text using regex.\n    \n    Returns:\n        List of (question, answer) tuples\n    \"\"\"\n    flashcards = []\n    pattern = r\"(?:^|\\n)Q:\\s*(.+?)\\nA:\\s*(.+?)(?=\\nQ:|\\n\\n|$)\"\n    matches = re.findall(pattern, text, flags=re.DOTALL)\n\n    for q, a in matches:\n        q_clean = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', q).strip()\n        a_clean = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', a).strip()\n        if q_clean and a_clean:\n            flashcards.append((q_clean, a_clean))\n    \n    return flashcards\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**8.3: Example Test**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"sample_text = \"\"\"\nNeural networks are powerful tools for pattern recognition, classification, and learning from data. \nThey form the backbone of modern AI applications like computer vision and natural language processing.\n\"\"\"\n\nresult = summarize_and_flashcards(sample_text)\n\nif not result[\"error\"]:\n    print(\"📝 Summary:\\n\", result[\"summary\"])\n    print(\"\\n🧠 Flashcards:\")\n    for i, (q, a) in enumerate(result[\"flashcards\"], 1):\n        print(f\"{i}. Q: {q}\\n   A: {a}\\n\")\nelse:\n    print(\"❌ Error:\", result[\"error\"])\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"| Feature          | Description                          |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| Summarization    | 3–5 sentence overview                |\n| Flashcards       | Q\\&A pairs, <20 words, context-based |\n| Output           | Dictionary (summary + flashcards)    |\n| Input truncation | Keeps within Gemini context window   |\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Part 9: Practice Question Generator\n\nGoal: Use Gemini to automatically generate practice-style questions (MCQs, descriptive, short answer) based on study material, such as:\n\nUploaded notes\n\nVideo transcripts\n\nExtracted PDFs or Excel questions","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**9.1: Function to Generate Practice Questions**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def generate_practice_questions(text: str, num_questions: int = 10) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generate practice questions using Gemini based on source material.\n    \n    Args:\n        text: Educational content or lecture transcript\n        num_questions: Number of questions to generate (default=10)\n    \n    Returns:\n        Dictionary with 'questions' and 'error' keys\n    \"\"\"\n    result = {\"questions\": [], \"error\": None}\n\n    try:\n        prompt = f\"\"\"\n**StudyMate Task: Question Generation**\n\nBelow is some study material. Based on it, generate {num_questions} diverse practice questions.\nUse at least 2 different formats (MCQ, Short Answer, True/False, Descriptive).\n\n=== MATERIAL START ===\n{text[:3000]}\n=== MATERIAL END ===\n\nRules:\n- Label each question by type (e.g., [MCQ], [Short Answer])\n- For MCQs, include 4 options and mark the correct one\n- Avoid duplication\n\"\"\"\n\n        response = gemini_model.generate_content(prompt)\n\n        if not response.text:\n            raise ValueError(\"No content returned.\")\n\n        result[\"questions\"] = extract_questions_from_text(response.text)\n\n    except Exception as e:\n        result[\"error\"] = f\"❌ Error generating questions: {str(e)}\"\n\n    return result\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**9.2: Helper Function to Clean Question Output**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def extract_questions_from_text(text: str) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Split Gemini response into clean question blocks.\n    \n    Returns:\n        List of question strings\n    \"\"\"\n    questions = [q.strip() for q in text.strip().split(\"\\n\\n\") if q.strip()]\n    return questions\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**9.3: Example Test Case**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"sample_notes = \"\"\"\nPhotosynthesis is the process by which green plants and some bacteria use sunlight to synthesize foods \nfrom carbon dioxide and water. It typically occurs in chloroplasts using chlorophyll.\n\"\"\"\n\nqa_result = generate_practice_questions(sample_notes, num_questions=5)\n\nif qa_result[\"error\"]:\n    print(qa_result[\"error\"])\nelse:\n    print(\"🧪 Practice Questions:\")\n    for i, q in enumerate(qa_result[\"questions\"], 1):\n        print(f\"{i}. {q}\\n\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"| Feature          | Description                                |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| Input            | Raw or cleaned educational text            |\n| Output           | MCQs, T/F, short answer, descriptive types |\n| Gemini Task Type | Instruction + prompt template              |\n| Result Format    | Labeled and formatted for direct use       |\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Part 10: Flashcard CSV Exporter\n\nGoal: Allow users to download flashcards as a CSV file for revision, import to Anki, or LMS tools.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**10.1: Export Flashcards to CSV File**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def export_flashcards_to_csv(flashcards: list, filename: str = \"flashcards.csv\") -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Save a list of (question, answer) flashcards to a CSV file.\n    \n    Args:\n        flashcards: List of tuples like [(Q1, A1), (Q2, A2), ...]\n        filename: Output filename (default = flashcards.csv)\n    \n    Returns:\n        Path to saved file or error message\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        with open(filename, mode='w', newline='', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n            writer = csv.writer(f)\n            writer.writerow([\"Question\", \"Answer\"])  # CSV header\n            writer.writerows(flashcards)\n        return f\"✅ Flashcards saved to {filename}\"\n    except Exception as e:\n        return f\"❌ Failed to export: {str(e)}\"\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**10.2: Example Usage**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Sample flashcards\nsample_flashcards = [\n    (\"What is the capital of France?\", \"Paris\"),\n    (\"Define photosynthesis.\", \"Process plants use to convert light into energy.\"),\n]\n\n# Export them\nprint(export_flashcards_to_csv(sample_flashcards, \"revision_cards.csv\"))\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"| Purpose                   | Use Case                            |\n| ------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| Anki Deck Import          | Upload to flashcard apps            |\n| LMS/Quiz Tool Integration | Reuse in Moodle, Google Forms, etc. |\n| Offline Revision          | Print and study                     |\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Part 11: LLM Output Evaluation\n\nGoal: Use Gemini to evaluate its own output (summary, flashcards, questions) for:\n\nRelevance to source\n\nConceptual clarity\n\nLanguage quality","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**11.1: Gemini-based Evaluator Function**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def evaluate_llm_output(source_text: str, generated_output: str, task_type: str = \"flashcards\") -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Evaluate generated flashcards, summary, or questions using Gemini.\n    \n    Args:\n        source_text: The original input document/text\n        generated_output: Text generated by LLM (summary, flashcards, etc.)\n        task_type: \"flashcards\", \"summary\", or \"questions\"\n    \n    Returns:\n        Evaluation feedback string\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        prompt = f\"\"\"\n**StudyMate Quality Evaluation**\n\nYou are an educational content evaluator.\n\nTask: Assess the {task_type} based on the original content.\nBe specific. Use 1–5 rating scale and give reasoned feedback.\n\n=== SOURCE TEXT ===\n{source_text[:2500]}\n\n=== LLM OUTPUT ===\n{generated_output[:2500]}\n\nRespond with:\n- Relevance Score (1–5)\n- Clarity Score (1–5)\n- Feedback Summary (1 paragraph)\n\"\"\"\n\n        evaluation_response = gemini_model.generate_content(prompt)\n\n        return evaluation_response.text.strip() if evaluation_response.text else \"❌ No evaluation returned.\"\n\n    except Exception as e:\n        return f\"❌ Evaluation error: {str(e)}\"\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**11.2: Example Test Case**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"source = \"\"\"\nPhotosynthesis is the biological process that converts solar energy into chemical energy. \nIt occurs in chloroplasts of green plants using chlorophyll pigments.\n\"\"\"\n\ngenerated_summary = \"\"\"\nPhotosynthesis is a process in which green plants use sunlight to make food from CO2 and water. \nThis occurs in chloroplasts using chlorophyll. It is vital for life on Earth.\n\"\"\"\n\n# Evaluate the summary\nfeedback = evaluate_llm_output(source, generated_summary, task_type=\"summary\")\nprint(\"🧪 Evaluation Feedback:\\n\", feedback)\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"| Criterion        | Meaning                                        |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| Relevance Score  | How well the generated output matches source   |\n| Clarity Score    | Readability, grammar, and conceptual soundness |\n| Feedback Summary | Qualitative explanation of score               |\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Part 12: StudyMate AI Chatbot + LangGraph Workflow\n\nGoal: Build a multi-tool GenAI chatbot using LangGraph and Gemini 1.5 Pro\nFeatures:\n\nStateful conversation loop\n\nTool use (summarization, flashcards, search, questions)\n\nMemory across steps (RAG + user query)","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**12.1: Define Custom Tool Functions for LangGraph**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"from langgraph.prebuilt import ToolNode\nfrom langgraph.graph import END\n\n# Define individual tools (wrapping earlier functions)\ndef tool_summarizer(input):\n    return summarize_and_flashcards(input[\"text\"])\n\ndef tool_question_gen(input):\n    return generate_practice_questions(input[\"text\"], num_questions=5)\n\ndef tool_rag_search(input):\n    return rag_search_verbose(input[\"query\"], k=3)\n\n# Map to LangGraph nodes\nsummarizer_node = ToolNode(tool_summarizer)\nquestion_node = ToolNode(tool_question_gen)\nsearch_node = ToolNode(tool_rag_search)\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**12.2: Define Stateful Node for Gemini 1.5 Chat**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"from langgraph.graph import StateGraph\n\n# Create a LangGraph state node using Gemini\n@LangGraph.node\ndef gemini_chat_node(state):\n    user_input = state[\"input\"]\n    context = state.get(\"retrieval_context\", \"\")\n    full_prompt = f\"{context}\\n\\n{user_input}\"\n    response = gemini_model.generate_content(full_prompt)\n    return {\"response\": response.text.strip()}\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**12.3: Build LangGraph Workflow**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Define the LangGraph flow\ngraph = StateGraph()\n\n# Add all nodes\ngraph.add_node(\"summarize\", summarizer_node)\ngraph.add_node(\"question\", question_node)\ngraph.add_node(\"search\", search_node)\ngraph.add_node(\"chat\", gemini_chat_node)\n\n# Define the edges (tool use before chat)\ngraph.set_entry_point(\"search\")\ngraph.add_edge(\"search\", \"summarize\")\ngraph.add_edge(\"summarize\", \"question\")\ngraph.add_edge(\"question\", \"chat\")\ngraph.add_edge(\"chat\", END)\n\n# Compile the graph\nstudy_graph = graph.compile()\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**12.4: Run the LangGraph**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"initial_input = {\n    \"input\": \"Explain what deep learning is and generate questions about it.\",\n    \"query\": \"deep learning\"\n}\n\noutput = study_graph.invoke(initial_input)\n\nprint(\"🧠 Chatbot Final Response:\\n\", output[\"response\"])\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"| Feature            | Benefit                        |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------ |\n| Modular            | Easily extend with new tools   |\n| Reusable memory    | Passes state between tools     |\n| Gemini integration | Uses Gemini Pro with grounding |\n| Tool chaining      | Summarize → Quiz → Chat        |\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# 12: StudyMate AI: Gradio Interface","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**Gradio Interface Code**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"import gradio as gr\n\n# Wrapper function for pipeline\ndef study_pipeline(file=None, link=None, task=\"Summarize + Flashcards\"):\n    try:\n        # Step 1: Load Text\n        if file is not None:\n            if file.name.endswith(\".pdf\"):\n                text = extract_pdf_text(file.name)\n            elif file.name.endswith(\".xlsx\"):\n                text = extract_excel_text(file)\n            else:\n                return \"❌ Unsupported file type.\"\n        elif link:\n            text = extract_text_from_youtube(link)\n        else:\n            return \"❌ Provide a file or a YouTube link.\"\n\n        # Step 2: Execute Task\n        if \"Summarize\" in task:\n            result = summarize_and_flashcards(text)\n            if result[\"error\"]: return result[\"error\"]\n            summary = result[\"summary\"]\n            cards = \"\\n\\n\".join([f\"Q: {q}\\nA: {a}\" for q, a in result[\"flashcards\"]])\n            return f\"📚 Summary:\\n\\n{summary}\\n\\n🧠 Flashcards:\\n\\n{cards}\"\n        \n        elif \"Questions\" in task:\n            result = generate_practice_questions(text)\n            if result[\"error\"]: return result[\"error\"]\n            return \"\\n\\n\".join(result[\"questions\"])\n        \n        elif \"Search\" in task:\n            return rag_search_verbose(link or \"deep learning\")\n\n        else:\n            return \"❌ Unknown task.\"\n\n    except Exception as e:\n        return f\"❌ Error: {str(e)}\"\n\n# Create UI\ngr.Interface(\n    fn=study_pipeline,\n    inputs=[\n        gr.File(label=\"Upload PDF/Excel (Optional)\"),\n        gr.Textbox(label=\"YouTube Link (Optional)\"),\n        gr.Radio(\n            [\"Summarize + Flashcards\", \"Practice Questions\", \"Semantic Search\"],\n            label=\"Task\"\n        )\n    ],\n    outputs=gr.Textbox(label=\"Output\"),\n    title=\"StudyMate AI - Smart Educational Assistant\",\n    description=\"Upload a file or paste a video link. Choose a task to generate summaries, flashcards, or quiz questions.\"\n).launch()\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"| Feature        | Description                        |\n| -------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| Upload Support | `.pdf`, `.xlsx` accepted           |\n| Link Input     | YouTube transcript compatible      |\n| Task Picker    | Summarization, Flashcards, QA, RAG |\n| Output Display | Dynamic generation in textbox      |\n","metadata":{}}]}